# create_proof flamegraph scaling experiment: raw per-run pipeline artifacts
# live on disk under scaling_runs/<config>/ but are not tracked here --
# pk/vk/srs/witness/compiled-circuit/logs are regenerable via
# scripts/run_scaling_rep.sh, and the actual flamegraph data
# (scaling_runs/<config>/pprof/repN.{folded,svg}) is kept on disk but is too
# large for git. Only the small aggregated results (scaling_runs/results/)
# are tracked.
/scaling_runs/*
!/scaling_runs/results/
!/scaling_runs/results/*.csv

# bench_stages.py / gen_models.py transformer-scaling benchmark + parse_ledger.py:
# results/<config>/{pk,vk}.key and kzg.srs are regenerable via bench_stages.py
# from settings.json + the pinned ezkl binary (see results/README.md), and are
# far too large for git (~100GB across the full sweep + quantization-scale
# variants -- pk.key alone reaches 36GB for the largest config). *.key is
# already excluded above; kzg.srs needs its own pattern since nothing else
# catches ".srs". Raw pprof .folded dumps (results/pprof/*.folded, ~380MB) are
# likewise regenerable (see results/PPROF_README.md) and not tracked.
# The blanket "*.csv" rule above would otherwise also hide the actual
# analysis output (summary.csv, op_ledger*.csv, prove_breakdown*.csv,
# models/MANIFEST.csv) -- re-included explicitly.
*.srs
results/pprof/*.folded
!results/*.csv
!results/**/*.csv
!models/MANIFEST.csv